              "Trump tweeted Wednesday night that the delay of two weeks came at China’s request and was “due to the fact that the People’s Republic of China will be celebrating their 70th Anniversary on October 1st.”",
              "Trump’s move came after China exempted 16 product lines from its retaliatory tariffs on U.S. goods earlier in the day. Observers have been quick to point out that the action by Beijing to ease tariffs on imports of U.S. pharmaceuticals, insecticides and other products was probably more self-serving than geared toward a detente in the trade war. China’s exemptions are similar to the U.S.’s “exclusion” process to ease some of the tariffs on American importers",
