              "One source close to the talks said deputy-level officials will start meeting next week to set up a potential preliminary deal involving agriculture purchases by China and, on the U.S. side, easing export restrictions on Huawei and potentially more delays to tariff increases. A primary focus is also likely to be how talks can proceed on core U.S. concerns related to intellectual property, currency, market access and other issues, the source said",
