              "Congressional aides for members of the USMCA working group confirmed they received USTR’s response and were going through it. But there were few other details available as of Wednesday night about the substance of Lighthizer’s reply. USTR would say only that “letters from Ambasador Lighthizer were delivered” on Wednesday",
              "**Gaining momentum?** Lighthizer is expected to talk by phone later this week with House Ways and Means Chairman Richard Neal, who leads the working group. And the trade rep is also slated to meet next week with the working group’s full membership, Rep. Jan Schakowsky (D-Ill.), who co-leads the group’s drug pricing team, told POLITICO.\n\n“The bottom line is there seems to be some movement,” Schakowsky said",
